    "body": "I think this needs to tie to \"sequence iteration\" more directly. Right now the normative definition of For each is still roughly \"performing a set of steps on each [item](https://whatpr.org/infra/451.html#list-item) in order\".\r\n\r\nMaybe\r\n\r\n> To **iterate** over a list _list_ performing steps _steps_ on each item, perform sequence iteration given _list_ and _steps_. This can also be (and usually is) written as \"For each _item_ of _list_: _steps_\".\r\n\r\nEdit: but see below, actually I think trying to share the code between lists and maps doesn't work well.",
